{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites","id":978361,"title":"Can Ghouls learn Cruac rites?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T07:03:44-07:00","id":978361,"title":"Can Ghouls learn Cruac rites?","content":"My assumption would be 'yes', given that Ghouls can learn the Disciplines of their Regnants, and there's even a section within the Ghoul book about 'Ghouls By Covenant'. Under the section detailing Ghouls within the Circle of the Crone, it states that &quot;For as much as potential thralls learn, however, they\u2019re still kept in the dark regarding the reality of the Circle and its Acolytes&quot;, until they're Ghouled.<br /> <br /> So my question stems from this:<br /> <br /> I have a ST character. She's Mekhet, and a member of the Circle with access to Cruac (which, in 2E, is treated as a Discipline, as is Theban Sorcery). Ghouls have the capability to learn and grow any Discipline their Regnant has. As Mekhet, this ST character has Auspex, Obfuscate, and Cruac as Disciplines. The rites themselves aren't Disciplines - they just use the dots in the Discipline as part of their roll to determine the success of the rite, just like with any other Discipline activation.<br /> <br /> So if this Mekhet wanted to bring her Ghoul into the fold of the Circle, and show her the rites (prompting this Ghoul into investing their XP into a dot or two in Cruac) is that possible? I haven't found anything that says that any Circle member MUST be Kindred, or that Cruac is a KINDRED specific 'Discipline'. My assumption would be to treat it as any other Discipline accessible to Ghouls - that as long as the Regnant has it, the Ghoul is able to learn it.<br /> <br /> Is my interpretation completely off? Have I missed something while reading to try to find the answer?<br /> <br /> Or is it really as simple as 'Yes, Ghouls can learn Cruac because the only 'requirement' is that Vitae is sacrificed, and, being Ghouls, they have the Vitae to do so?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:43:16-07:00","id":978394,"title":"","content":"As it's written in 2nd edition no they can't. Cruac rituals involve spilling vitae and the book expressly calls out the fact that ghouls can't use any power that entails spilling vitae. There's also the fact that they don't have the requisite Humanity to sacrifice in order to learn Cruac at all. But I'm sure those details can be ST fiated away by saying they sold their soul to a Strix, who are often credited as being an origin source of Cruac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T07:47:20-07:00","id":978398,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for pointing this out to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:21:25-07:00","id":978570,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that they can't <i>use</i> Disciplines that require spilling blood.<br /> <br /> They can still <i>learn </i>them. Only Coils and Scales are specifically called out as impossible for Ghouls to learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:09:14-07:00","id":978663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=978570#post978570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that they can't <i>use</i> Disciplines that require spilling blood.<br /> <br /> They can still <i>learn </i>them. Only Coils and Scales are specifically called out as impossible for Ghouls to learn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was debating doing a plot thread like this where two different Acolyte cults are fighting over a ghoul who knows how to preform a rare Cruac ritual. Both sides want to learn the fine points of the ritual, and only the Ghoul is capable of teaching a key aspect of it (as a result, the player characters get enlisted to kidnap the ghoul). I don't think this is exactly canon, but I was wondering if there would be some internally consistent way to make that work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5106-umoja","name":"Umoja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:14:26-07:00","id":978667,"title":"","content":"Some rituals require Vitae, but not necessarily from the performer of said ritual.<br /> That said, ghouls are usually seen as a lesser form of &quot;life&quot; than Kindred and even though they may be treated with some margin of courtesy, they NOT equals. The Circle tends to take this a step further with their reverence for vampirism itself, though who knows what spin any individual cult may place on ideas such as these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:54:03-07:00","id":978685,"title":"","content":"All rituals, when using Cruac, require at least one point of Vitae from the ritualist. The rest can come from either the ritualist or another vampire (willing or not). Mortal blood doesn't work for Cruac.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's really unlikely that a Ghoul would be allowed to learn rituals. One that did would probably be targeted for murder like if a non-Crone learned a Cruac ritual.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the idea of a Ghoul with a rare ritual is a really neat idea and works mechanically by RAW. You just might want to add another player into the mix that wants the ghoul dead for knowing Circle secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:33:38-07:00","id":978762,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, I forgot about that when reading some that mentioned the additional cost in the text of the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:55:54-07:00","id":978831,"title":"","content":"While it's first edition material, one way to have ghouls using cruac is the sons of phobos- mortal occultists who gain vitae for cruac rituals through human sacrifice, and being a son of phobos was specifically mentioned as compatible with ghouldom.<br /> <br /> Or really throw people for a loop, have ghouls with their own form of blood magic that isn't cruac or theban sorcery- The Phanariots, witches who use their magic to become ghouls and control their &quot;masters,&quot; again first edition material, and optional to boot, but a fun option I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:13:27-07:00","id":978856,"title":"","content":"Just because you can't do something doesn't mean you don't know how. Also the fact that ghouls can't perform Cruac rituals, in spite of knowing them, could be part of why Kindred consider them lesser. The ghoul could have served a Cruac master in performing rituals (...hand me that knife...fetch the bowl... did you get the chicken like I told you?) and learned the mechanics through keen observation. He might even have been chosen for ghouling because of his knack or background in such areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:23:33-07:00","id":978862,"title":"","content":"Per page 151 of 2E, the first point of Vitae for a ritual is spent as if the user was performing any other discipline, while the rest must be spilled from blood sacrifice, but doesn't have to come from the performer.<br /> <br /> Ghouls aren't forbidden from learning Cruac by RAW, and could even perform 1 dot Rites themselves. Anything beyond that would require the sacrifice to come from a different source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:28:38-07:00","id":978864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=978862#post978862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per page 151 of 2E, the first point of Vitae for a ritual is spent as if the user was performing any other discipline, while the rest must be spilled from blood sacrifice, but doesn't have to come from the performer.<br /> <br /> Ghouls aren't forbidden from learning Cruac by RAW, and could even perform 1 dot Rites themselves. Anything beyond that would require the sacrifice to come from a different source.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My thoughts exactly. Given this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Cr\u00faac rites cost one Vitae per dot of the rite. The first Vitae<br /> is spent by the caster as though fueling a Discipline. Any<br /> remaining Vitae used must be spilled in the ritual\u2019s casting,<br /> and not necessarily by the caster...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, given that this Ghoul had a Regnant who was either particularly invested in their learning the rites (like you pointed out, probably limited to 1 dot rites) or for whatever other personal reason found it important for their Ghoul to know certain ones, like... Rigor Mortis, it would (in my opinion) be perfectly reasonable and valid for the caster (the Ghoul in this case) to SPEND the Vitae to 'fuel' the 'Discipline', and then have their Regnant on standby, willing to SPILL any actual sacrificial blood required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:31:10-07:00","id":978865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tenebra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=978864#post978864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, given that this Ghoul had a Regnant who was either particularly invested in their learning the rites (like you pointed out, probably limited to 1 dot rites) or for whatever other personal reason found it important for their Ghoul to know certain ones, like... Rigor Mortis, it would (in my opinion) be perfectly reasonable and valid for the caster (the Ghoul in this case) to SPEND the Vitae to 'fuel' the 'Discipline', and then have their Regnant on standby, willing to SPILL any actual sacrificial blood required.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then the Circle probably comes to kill them both, as mentioned above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:31:56-07:00","id":978867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=978865#post978865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then the Circle probably comes to kill them both, as mentioned above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, it's never a good chronicle unless someone's trying to kill someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:29:48-07:00","id":978900,"title":"","content":"Cruac also has the thing, where you could use human sacrifice to satisfy the remaining.. .so imagine a couple of rogue ghouls, hunting down vampires for sustenance, while also getting humans to fuel cruac...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T04:09:00-07:00","id":978943,"title":"","content":"Ghouls with Cruac can do \u2022 rituals no problem because they only cost 1 vitae, which is payed for like a normal discipline, so no problem.<br /> <br /> Ghouls can learn higher dots of Cruac and rituals, but they need to use a Vampire or something with its own vitae, to spill its blood for \u2022\u2022 or higher rituals, but that Vampire need not be CoC Vampires.<br /> <br /> More often a Ghoul with \u2022\u2022+ Cruac dots are going to be used helping their bosses as supporting the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:00:36-07:00","id":979021,"title":"","content":"You cannot use mortal blood for Cruac, so no human sacrifice unless you drink them then spill it from the vampire.<br /> <br /> Ghouls count as mortal for the purposes of feeding (suggesting to me that their blood is still mortal blood, though they can't spill their own for rites in any case), so I think it's debatable whether their blood functions. Debatable just means that an ST can interpret it either way, however, so whatever you prefer.<br /> <br /> That said, there's another nifty hook in the Blood Sorcery section that you might use for your Ghoul ritualist: those that practice rites outside the protection of the Circle tend to end up with bad luck or visits from Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:07:40-07:00","id":979028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=979021#post979021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot use mortal blood for Cruac, so no human sacrifice unless you drink them then spill it from the vampire.<br /> <br /> Ghouls count as mortal for the purposes of feeding (suggesting to me that their blood is still mortal blood, though they can't spill their own for rites in any case), so I think it's debatable whether their blood functions. Debatable just means that an ST can interpret it either way, however, so whatever you prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pff.. I hate to admit, but you're right. Anyways, I'll certainly allow Human Sacrifice to produce some vitae for Cruac (even if it's just 1/kill) to make higher rating Cruac possible for Ghouls. But that's a house rule. <br /> <br /> Just to make my plot hook work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:21:41-07:00","id":979097,"title":"","content":"I do recall, in 1E, Ghouls beiing called out as having the *ability* to perform Cruac rituals.. but that certain ones were a good way to commit very elaborate magical suicide. Turning yourblood to poison, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T09:58:53-07:00","id":979126,"title":"","content":"Ghouls were also more expensive to create, maintain and control in 1st edition. Now they're cheap to create and maintain, not so easy to control and easier to lose control over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:26:33-07:00","id":979196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tenebra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites#post978361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they have the Vitae to do so?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls have Vitae to <i>Spend</i>, but not <i>Spill</i>. It must be Vitae Spilled not mortal blood, so human sacrifice without a vampire intermediary to drink the blood to convert it to Vitae and then Spill wouldn't work. Alternatively, a Vampire Sacrifice would work just fine, so that is a fun idea. Thus a Ghoul Cruac ritualist with vampires slaves made to Spill their Vitae either through violent sacrifice, horrific arcane medical procedures (-cough-Ordo Dracul/Cheiron Group-cough-), or through compliance of orders given, is entirely possible and is likely happening somewhere within the world where the Chronicles of Darkness takes place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:37:02-07:00","id":979204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=979126#post979126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls were also more expensive to create, maintain and control in 1st edition. Now they're cheap to create and maintain, not so easy to control and easier to lose control over.</div> </div> </div> </div>3rd stage blood bond with severe addiction is the definition of control. They are obsessively enthralled, compulsively needy, otherwords, madly, wildly in love with you. Hurting you emotionally or physically is a Breaking point at -5 or humanity 1. That is the equivalent of mass murder and most people wouldn't even dream of committing such a crime. <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=979196#post979196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls have Vitae to <i>Spend</i>, but not <i>Spill</i>. It must be Vitae Spilled not mortal blood, so human sacrifice without a vampire intermediary to drink the blood to convert it to Vitae and then Spill wouldn't work. Alternatively, a Vampire Sacrifice would work just fine, so that is a fun idea. Thus a Ghoul Cruac ritualist with vampires slaves made to Spill their Vitae either through violent sacrifice, horrific arcane medical procedures (-cough-Ordo Dracul/Cheiron Group-cough-), or through compliance of orders given, is entirely possible and is likely happening somewhere within the world where the Chronicles of Darkness takes place.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I have to add is that the vampire would have to be willing. Vitae just doesn't fall out when a vampire is cut. It's not like blood in that way. They have to will it to leave their bodies, even if they get their arm chopped off, it would only pool at the wound and not hit the ground.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of exceptions: vampire Feeding, Dracul stuff, or the Kindred fighting merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:41:06-07:00","id":979210,"title":"","content":"If you want to know what non-vampires with Cruac look like, check out the Sons of Phobos in <i>Blood Sorcery</i>. (Though note that they're hella destructive.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:02:03-07:00","id":979565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/978361-can-ghouls-learn-cruac-rites?p=979210#post979210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to know what non-vampires with Cruac look like, check out the Sons of Phobos in <i>Blood Sorcery</i>. (Though note that they're hella destructive.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have definitely been reading up in Blood Sorcery (can't believe it took me this long to read, because it's a useful af book). <br /> <br /> Thanks, all, for your input. You've all been super helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}